  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 230 AM MST TUE NOV 3 2026\nA trough will move onto the British Columbia coast on Friday \nwhile a ridge off the coast of California builds inland and \nnorth. The ridge should keep atmospheric river moisture \nassociated with the trough to the north with only a 10-20% \nchance of showers across our northern areas on Friday. This \ngeneral pattern will hold through the weekend and into early \nnext week, keeping our area mostly dry while southwest flow \nincreases temperatures to 5-10 degrees above normal. Lower \nvalleys will see highs in the 60s with 40s and 50s in the \nmountains. The trough will edge further down the coast on \nSunday, bringing breezy conditions and increased clouds but a \nless than 10% chance of precipitation. Precipitation chances \nwill climb to 10-30% by Tuesday as this pattern progresses.",
